FIXED: Clash no longer takes exponential time and memory normalizing `foldl`/`scanl` over a vector when the fold result keeps the (co-recursively defined) vector spine alive, e.g. `snd (foldl const (z, s) (xs :: Vec n a))`. The evaluator's `zipWith` reduction now shares its arguments instead of duplicating the vector spine on every peel. See [#3308](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/issues/3308).
